LevelDB for applications, through its own C API.

zebkit exports LevelDB as it exports the other libraries in the engine. Its C
API is db/c.cc, which Chromium does not build. Two things stop it being usable
in an application's process: compactions go to the browser's thread pool, which
an application that has not started the engine does not have; and names are
converted through UTF-8 with the locale, which is the application's, so a
non-ASCII path fails under the C locale. Without a thread pool a compaction
runs on a thread of its own, and on POSIX a name is the path's own bytes.
Chromium's names are already that under a UTF-8 locale.

